* 0x0D = 

* 0x0E = Output the (G,X,Y) triple.

* 0x0F = Output the (G,X,Y) triple and stop.

Instruction opcodes 0x40 to 0x7F works as follows:

* Bit5-bit4 = The number of the X or Y register that will be modified by
this instruction.

* Bit3 = Set to use X/Y as input or clear to use G as input.

* Bit2 = Set to use Y or clear to use X. (This affects both the input
register selection and the output register selection.)

* Bit1-bit0 = The number of the G or X or Y register to use as input.

The second byte of the instruction then uses the format:

* Bit7-bit6 = If bit3 of the first byte is clear, then it is one less than
the multiplier, but if set then this selects which metric to use, which can
be: 0(advancement), 1(negative extent), 2(positive extent), 3(extra). (The
meaning of the metrics, and how the metrics are calculated, depends on the
font format.)

* Bit5-bit4 = Rounding: 0(none), 1(down), 2(up), 3(default).

* Bit3 = Send output before making the change to X or Y.

* Bit2-bit0 = Kind of calculation.

